  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Subaru Outback?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device installed. The Telemetry API returns fuel level as a percentage and in liters when you query with a Vehicle JWT for that vehicle."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Subaru Outback with no connected services?",
      "a": "Install a DIMO device and have the owner share the vehicle with your app. Exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Subaru Outback?",
      "a": "Use the Telemetry API segments query with the idling detection mechanism, which requires a DIMO device. It treats contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range as segments, and the maxIdleRpm setting (default 1000) adjusts the threshold."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Subaru Outback mileage?",
      "a": "With a DIMO device supplying the odometer, call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT. You then retrieve the resulting attestation through the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect refuel events on a Subaru Outback?",
      "a": "Use the Telemetry API segments query with the refuel mechanism on a vehicle with a DIMO device. It detects where fuel level rises significantly, and minIncreasePercent (default 15) sets the minimum rise."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Subaru Outback, that data comes through a DIMO device, with coverage for model years 2010 and newer. Coverage for this model is tested rather than expected, and no coverage gaps are noted. Once the owner shares the vehicle, you query its signals through the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT."
